  "resources": {
    "costumbres": {
      "c-238d268adfbb7753": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-643",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "Some have thought from these words that it was customary, literally, to sound a trumpet before an alms-giver. However this might have been in the streets, it certainly could not be permitted “in the synagogues,” as it would disturb the services there. There is no evidence whateve…"
      },
      "c-83b3a47ba6e6c1ca": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-644",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "This is a proverbial expression, found also in classic and Rabbinical authors. We know of no custom alluded to in this proverb save the general habit of giving with the right hand, as it is more conveniently used than the other; but Mr. Jowett speaks of a custom lie noticed in Pa…"
      },
      "c-8de5a318aac6d4fa": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-646",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "See also Luke 12:29. So great is the scarcity of fuel that even dried grass and withered flowers are used for making a fire. They are carefully gathered and carried in bundles, sometimes in the arms, and sometimes loaded on donkeys. See also note on 1 Kings 17:10 and on Psalm 58:…"
      },
      "c-b827e5829b6cd212": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-645",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "Some of the rabbis in our Lord’s time had taught that oft-repeated prayers were of certain efficacy, thus falling into an imitation of the heathen, who have ever been noted for unmeaning repetitions. When Elijah challenged the worshipers of Baal, they called on their god “from mo…"
      }
    },
